# 800-KRN-0137 — `link` may make one endpoint, for its programs' output — done

**Type:** `init` · **Owner:** kernel session · **Priority:** P1 · **Status:** done (2026-10-21) · **Blocked by:** — · **Main task:** [800](../issues/800-mind-link.md) (the link track's) · **Constitution:** MC-3.13

## Problem

The link track's request of 2026-10-20 (`internal-dev-messages`, `KRN/2026-10-20T2029Z-LNK-link-needs-an-endpoint-quota-of-one.md`), for 800-LNK-0009:
- **How output reaches `link`.** A program prints into `SLOT_CONSOLE` (`mind::output`), and `link` grants each program it starts a send copy of an endpoint of its own there, as `console` does.
- **Why it fails.** `init` gives `link` no endpoint quota, so `Endpoint::create()` fails with `ERR_LIMIT` and RUN is refused.

## Plan

`init` gives `link` a quota of one endpoint, as the updater has (`"link" => Quota { endpoints: 1, ..Quota::default() }`).
- No grant, no capability, no ABI change.
- `link` makes the endpoint only when `link.conf` holds `run`.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The link track's `link` suite (on its branch, 800-LNK-0009) starts a program from `data/link/` through `mindlink run` and reads its output to its end, on an image with this change.
- [x] The gate passes.

## Resolution

- **Where.** `init/src/main.rs`, the quotas: `"link" => Quota { endpoints: 1, ..Quota::default() }`.
- **Shown in gate g0141** (`main` f7c64d7, every group passed). With `run` in `link.conf`, the link track's `link` suite on x86:
  - started a program from `data/link/t/` twice through `mindlink run`;
  - read its output to its end on `link`'s own endpoint;
  - found `link`'s granted capabilities unchanged.

